// Deliberately a bad rule: alerting on one exact SHA256 value only ever
// matches this one sample, never the technique itself -- a single
// changed byte defeats it entirely. Included on purpose to demonstrate
// Local Detections Import's behavior on an "improper" rule: it still
// gets cataloged and browsable (nothing silently disappears), but the
// top-of-results alert flags it as invalid and explains exactly why.
DeviceFileEvents
| where SHA256 == "185755788d69c83979c75f27535483f3da7e9ee32b641f58cb6fccfd6bd77077"
